# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Green Turtle Kava — store checkout
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The /checkout flow creates a Stripe Checkout Session server-side and redirects
# the customer to Stripe's hosted, PCI-compliant payment page. Set your Stripe
# SECRET key here for local dev, and add it as an Environment Variable in Vercel
# for production. Never commit the real key.
#
# Test key looks like:  sk_test_...        Live key looks like:  sk_live_...
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keystatic CMS — production only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In local dev (`npm run dev`) Keystatic uses `kind: 'local'` storage and writes
# straight to disk, so none of these are needed. In production it uses
# `kind: 'github'` and commits to AdopsMarketing/GreenTurtleKava, which needs a
# GitHub App.
#
# Create the app from the running site: deploy first, visit
# https://greenturtlekava.co/keystatic and follow the setup screen — it creates
# the GitHub App and prints these values. Add all four to the Vercel project's
# Environment Variables, then redeploy. See docs/keystatic-events.md.
KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Any random 32+ character string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`
KEYSTATIC_SECRET=
# The GitHub App's slug, e.g. green-turtle-kava-cms
PUBLIC_KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
